    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\nI have been using the following snippet in both nvim and vim for years and it has been working well until recently I did one more switch to start using `mini.clue` from `which-key.nvim`\n\n```vimscript\n\" execute macro at visual range, does not stop when no match\nfunction! ExecuteMacroOverVisualRange()\n    echo \"@\".getcmdline()\n    execute \":'<,'>normal @\".nr2char(getchar())\nendfunction\nxnoremap @ :<C-u>call ExecuteMacroOverVisualRange()<CR>\n```\n\neven with a minimal mini.clue setup\n\n```lua\nlocal miniclue = require(\"mini.clue\")\nminiclue.setup({\n  triggers = {\n    { mode = \"n\", keys = \"<Leader>\" },\n  },\n})\n```\n\nwithout miniclue in use, i can visually select a range and apply the macro. When in use, the macro just failed silently. \nI suspect this has to do with how mini.clue intercepts the keystrokes but not sure if this is a bug. \n\nThanks in advance!",
