        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I think the reason is that [`@` and `Q` are remapped during `require('mini.clue').setup()`](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/402ee6c6ec8ea44b22330446c8fb4e615fd3953e/doc/mini-clue.txt#L90-L91) to temporarily disable triggers when executing a macro. If that is not done, there are some troubles with duplicating keys during macro replay if it includes triggers.\n\nThere is an almost three years old PR into Neovim (neovim/neovim#24565) that would make those mappings obsolete (and the PR was created as a result of 'mini.clue' development), but it has not yet gained traction, unfortunately.\n\nI am really hesitant about changing anything implementation related in 'mini.clue', because it is a rather fragile experience to make it work. My only current suggestion would be to try and use `\":'<,'>normal! @\"` (i.e. with `!`) to execute default `@`. This seems to work, but would probably bring problems if the macro contains a trigger keys. I am afraid this is the best I can suggest here, sorry.",
